<<set _opts to [["split","The FBI says it knows who did it, but nobody knows where the art is"],["soon","The FBI knows who did it, so the art will turn up soon"],["nothing","Nobody has any idea who did it"]]>>
<div class="choices"><<for _o range _opts>><<capture _o>><span @class="$ww is _o[0] ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _o[1]>><<set $ww to _o[0]>><<replace "#wws">><<include "WWList">><</replace>><<replace "#file">><<include "ReportButton">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div>


:: LeadList
<<set _opts to [["philly","The attempted sale around 2002 that the FBI mentioned"],["letter","Find the 1994 letter-writer"],["vault","Search for the billionaire's secret vault"]]>>
<div class="choices"><<for _o range _opts>><<capture _o>><span @class="$lead is _o[0] ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _o[1]>><<set $lead to _o[0]>><<replace "#leadlist">><<include "LeadList">><</replace>><<replace "#file">><<include "ReportButton">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div>


:: ReportButton
<<if $ww is "" or $lead is "">><p class="note">Answer both questions to file your report.</p>
<<else>><div class="actions">[[File my report|Verdict]]</div><</if>>


:: Verdict [nobar]
<<set _thOk to setup.theories.map(function(t){ return $th[t.id] === t.answer && (t.answer !== "out" || t.needs.some(function(n){ return $notebook.includes(n); })); })>>
<<set _s1 to _thOk.every(function(x){ return x; })>>
<<set _susOk to setup.suspects.map(function(s){ return s.keys[$key[s.id]][1]; })>>
<<set _s2 to _susOk.every(function(x){ return x; })>>
<<set _s3 to $ww is "split" and $notebook.includes("fbi2013")>>
<<set _s4 to $lead is "philly" and $notebook.includes("philly")>>
<<set $stars to (_s1 ? 1 : 0) + (_s2 ? 1 : 0) + (_s3 ? 1 : 0) + (_s4 ? 1 : 0)>>
<<set $deductions to $notebook.filter(function(id){ return setup.cards[id].type === "deduction"; }).length>>
<<if $stars is 4>><div class="stamp solved">Report accepted</div><<else>><div class="stamp">Report filed</div><</if>>
<h2>Detective rating: <<print $stars>> of 4 stars</h2>
<ul class="stars">
<li @class="_s1 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s1 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>The theory board.</b> <<if _s1>>You ruled out three theories with evidence, and kept two that nobody can rule out.<<else>>Here's how the evidence sorts them:<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s2 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s2 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Checkable evidence.</b> <<if _s2>>For every suspect, you picked evidence that could actually be checked.<<else>>Some of your picks were beliefs or memories that can't be checked. See below.<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s3 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s3 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Who vs. where.</b> <<if _s3>>Exactly: knowing who isn't the same as knowing where.<<elseif $ww is "split">>Right idea, but you never read the FBI's statement that backs it up.<<elseif $ww is "soon">>The FBI said that in 2013, and the art still hasn't turned up. Knowing who doesn't tell you where.<<else>>The FBI says it does know who. It just hasn't found the art.<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s4 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s4 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>The next lead.</b> <<if _s4>>The most recent real trail the FBI has described. That's where the art was last thought to be.<<elseif $lead is "philly">>Good pick, but you never found the FBI statement about it.<<elseif $lead is "letter">>That writer went silent in 1994 and never came back. It's a cold trail.<<else>>That's a guess from a radio caller, not a lead.<</if>></li>
</ul>
<<if not _s1>><ul class="theory-key"><<for _i to 0; _i lt setup.theories.length; _i++>><<set _t to setup.theories[_i]>><li @class="_thOk[_i] ? 'ok' : 'no'"><b><<print _t.text>>:</b> <<print _t.answer is "out" ? "ruled out" : "still possible">>. <<print _t.why>><<if _t.answer is "out" and $th[_t.id] is "out" and not _thOk[_i]>> (You didn't collect the clue that proves it.)<</if>></li><</for>></ul><</if>>
<ul class="theory-key"><<for _i to 0; _i lt setup.suspects.length; _i++>><<set _s to setup.suspects[_i]>><li @class="_susOk[_i] ? 'ok' : 'no'"><b><<print _s.name>>:</b> you picked “<<print _s.keys[$key[_s.id]][0]>>.” <<print _s.note>></li><</for>></ul>
<p class="meta">Deductions worked out: <<print $deductions>> of <<print setup.dedTotal>></p>
<h3>Your notebook, flipped over</h3>
<<if $notebook.length is 0>><p class="note">You didn't collect any cards.</p><<else>>
<div class="cards reveal"><<for _id range $notebook>><div @class="'card ' + (setup.cards[_id].type === 'claim' ? 'single' : setup.cards[_id].type)"><span class="tag"><<print setup.typeLabel[setup.cards[_id].type]>></span><span class="card-title"><<print setup.cards[_id].title>></span></div><</for>></div><</if>>
<div class="actions">[[What's known today|RealHistory]]</div>


:: RealHistory [nobar]
<h2>What's known today</h2>
<p>The 13 works have never been found. The museum still offers $10 million for information that brings them back, and the empty frames still hang in their places.</p>
<p>The FBI says it knows who the thieves were and that both are dead, but it has never officially named them. In 2026, the FBI agent who led the case for more than 20 years published a book naming the men he believes were involved. He believes the art still exists and will surface someday.</p>
<p>The real investigators are in the same spot you are: a good idea of who, and no idea of where.</p>
<div class="lesson">
<h3>Your lesson as a trainee</h3>
<ul>
<li>"Who did it?" and "Where is it?" are different questions.</li>
<li>A claim nobody can check isn't proof, and neither is suspicion.</li>
<li>Rule things out with evidence. What's left is still possible, not proven.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<p class="note">Made up for this game: the director, the lawyer and the radio callers. The suspects, statements, letter, warehouse, reward and searches are based on the real case.</p>
<div class="actions">[[Finish case|CaseClosed]]</div>


:: CaseClosed [nobar]
<<include "Banner">>
<<run setup.reportResult()>>
<div class="stamp solved big">Case closed</div>
<h2>Case 003, Part 2 complete</h2>
<p>Detective rating: <b><<print $stars>> of 4</b>. Deductions: <b><<print $deductions>> of <<print setup.dedTotal>></b>.</p>
<p>Tell Rocky where you think the art is, how sure you are, and your detective rating.</p>
<div class="actions secondary"><<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>></div>


